## Shopify SEO questions

### What can't be changed in Shopify, and what can?

You cannot change the fixed URL prefixes: `/products/`, `/collections/`, `/pages/` and `/blogs/`. Products also stay reachable through a second URL inside a collection. Canonical tags handle that.

You can change almost everything after the prefix. That includes product and collection handles, page titles and meta descriptions, collection copy, internal linking, structured data through your theme, and URL redirects. Shopify generates robots.txt automatically, and you can customise it through the theme within limits. I tell you which fixes are possible on your theme before you pay for them.

### What if I am moving to Shopify from another platform?

Plan the SEO before you launch. Every old URL needs a redirect to its new Shopify URL. The content that earns rankings needs to carry over. My [SEO migration](/services/seo-migration-consultant/) service covers the redirect map, staging checks and launch-day checks. The migration audit starts from £495.

### Do you work on Shopify Plus?

Yes. Plus gives more control over checkout, API access and multi-currency storefronts. I adapt the work to that, particularly for international SEO and structured data.

